# Pad A presses north, unbound, so the slot is its own, and Pad B's
# press of east takes nothing over. A leaves while B waits, holding east:
# B stands in at once, and the Resync presses Space. Stick motion does
# not make the slot B's, so when A comes back before B presses a button,
# A takes the slot back: B's east is let go of and B waits again, first
# in line. A has the slot provisionally again until its south, which taps
# Ctrl+Z; B's release does nothing. When A leaves again, B stands in
# again.
